</script>

<Doc>
    <p>Most of them are <code>Reactive</code>, which is what makes them readable by name and
    reactive to read — <code>{'{online}'}</code> in a template mounts and unmounts a banner with no
    listener attached.</p>

    <Section title="Scope, not globals">
        <p>An ambient is <strong>request-local on a server</strong> and process-wide in a browser.
        That is the whole of what keeps two callers apart: <code>principal</code> inside a handler
        is the principal of the request that reached it, and there is no moment at which one
        request's is visible to another's.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`request`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>request</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; Request</code></td><td>The request being served.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`response`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>response</code></td><td><code>{'() => { status: number; headers: Headers }'}</code></td><td>The response being built for the request being served.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`cookies`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>cookies</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; CookieMap</code></td><td>The cookies of the request being served, live and mutable.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`route`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>route.url</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;URL&gt;</code></td><td>Where we are.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>route.params</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;Params&gt;</code></td><td>The matched route's segments.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Params</code></td><td><code>Record&lt;string, string | string[]&gt;</code></td><td>What a matched route's segments are.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>route.name</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;string&gt;</code></td><td>The resolution path.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>route.navigating</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;boolean&gt;</code></td><td>Whether a navigation is in flight.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`online`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>online</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;boolean&gt;</code></td><td>Whether the caller can reach the app.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`principal`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>principal.authenticated</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;boolean&gt;</code></td><td>Whether this caller presented something the server accepted.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>principal.expiresAt</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;string | undefined&gt;</code></td><td>When the seal lapses.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>principal.error</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;Failed&lt;string, unknown&gt; | undefined&gt;</code></td><td>The app's resolver having failed.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>principal.resolved</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;Principal&gt;</code></td><td>What <code>onPrincipal</code> returned, merged over the baseline.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>principal.caller</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;string&gt;</code></td><td>Which browser, as against who they are.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>principal.set</code></td><td><code>(claims: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;) =&gt; Promise&lt;void&gt;</code></td><td>Authenticates this caller.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>principal.clear</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; void</code></td><td>Signs this caller out.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Principal</code></td><td><code>{'interface Principal { [claim: string]: unknown; authenticated: boolean; expiresAt?: string; error?: Failed<string, unknown> }'}</code></td><td>The wire document.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>authenticated</code></td><td><code>boolean</code></td><td>Whether this caller presented a seal the server accepted.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>expiresAt</code></td><td><code>string | undefined</code></td><td>When the seal lapses.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>error</code></td><td><code>Failed&lt;string, unknown&gt; | undefined</code></td><td>The app's resolver having failed.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`config`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>config</code></td><td><code>Reactive&lt;Config&gt;</code></td><td>The resolved configuration document.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Config</code></td><td><code>{'interface Config { [field: string]: unknown; APP_NAME: string; APP_VERSION: string; APP_DATA_DIR: string }'}</code></td><td>The resolved document, which an app widens with fields of its own by declaration merging.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Env</code></td><td><code>Record&lt;string, string | undefined&gt;</code></td><td>The process environment as read, before coercion.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>config.invalidate</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; void</code></td><td>Re-reads the environment and reruns <code>onConfig</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>onConfig</code></td><td><code>(fn: ConfigDefaults | null, options?: ConfigOptions) =&gt; () =&gt; void</code></td><td>The app's defaults and its schema.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>ConfigDefaults</code></td><td><code>(env: Env) =&gt; unknown</code></td><td>The defaults function, synchronous by contract.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>schema</code></td><td><code>Schema&lt;Config&gt;</code></td><td>The gate over the whole configuration document.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`trace`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>trace</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; string</code></td><td>The trace id of the operation this work belongs to.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>trace.sampled</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; boolean</code></td><td>The caller's sampling decision, carried through verbatim.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>trace.span</code></td><td><code>{'<T>(name: string, body: () => T, options?: { timing?: boolean }) => T'}</code></td><td>Opens a child span around a body.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>trace.headers</code></td><td><code>() =&gt; Record&lt;string, string&gt;</code></td><td>What an outbound request carries.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`server`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>server</code></td><td><code>&lt;WebSocketData&gt;() =&gt; Server&lt;WebSocketData&gt;</code></td><td>The listening server.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`health`">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Signature</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>health</code></td><td><code>Rpc&lt;Health, undefined&gt;</code></td><td>The account of the app this call is in.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Health</code></td><td><code>{'interface Health { version: string; abide: string; startedAt: string }'}</code></td><td>The account itself, which an app widens with what its <code>onHealth</code> adds.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>onHealth</code></td><td><code>(report: () =&gt; unknown | Promise&lt;unknown&gt;) =&gt; () =&gt; void</code></td><td>The app's reporter, merged over the baseline.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>version</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>The app's version.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>abide</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>The framework's version.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>startedAt</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>When the process started, ISO-8601.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p><code>health</code> is the one name here that is called rather than read:
        <code>health()</code> on either side, and the call is what asks. Nothing loads the account
        for a page that never calls it.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Description">
        <Section title="Isomorphism is per value, not per name" level={3}>
            <p>Each of these answers from what the side it is on actually has, and the table on its
            own page says how. <code>online</code> is <code>navigator.onLine</code> and its events
            in a browser and <code>true</code> on a server, a caller being served having reached the
            app. <code>request</code> exists only where a request does.</p>

            <p>That is not a shim: a name means the same <strong>question</strong> on both sides and
            is answered from different evidence, which is why a page rendered on the server and
            hydrated in a browser can read one without branching on where it is.</p>
        </Section>

        <Section title="Reading one subscribes" level={3}>
            <p>An ambient that is a <code>Reactive</code> is read the way any value is read, so
            reading it in a template subscribes and reading it in a handler does not. Nothing about
            it being ambient changes the tracking rules.</p>
        </Section>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Examples">
        <Section title="The caller, in a rung" level={3}>
            <Code language="abide" caption="src/invoices/page.abide — excerpt" code={`<script server>
export const voidInvoice = POST(
    ({ id }: { id: string }) => database.invoice.void(id),
    {
        middleware: [
            (next, ctx) => {
                if (!principal.authenticated()) return refuse(401)
                return next(ctx)
            },
        ],
    },
)
</script>`} />
        </Section>

        <Section title="The route, in a layout" level={3}>
            <Code language="abide" caption="src/layout.abide — excerpt" code={`<nav aria-busy={route.navigating}>
    <a href="/invoices"
        aria-current={route.name.startsWith('invoices')}>Invoices</a>
</nav>`} />
        </Section>

        <Section title="Telling a reader the connection went" level={3}>
            <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`{#if !online}
    <p role="status">You are offline. Nothing is being saved.</p>
{/if}`} />
        </Section>
    </Section>

